<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Roosevelt returns four weeks after changing from albuterol alone to budesonide-formoterol two inhalations twice daily plus one as needed. He is much better: daytime symptoms on two or three days a week instead of most days, night waking once in four weeks, and he finishes his boxing rounds. He has used 4 to 6 as-needed inhalations a week, mostly before training. The dose counter matches about 90 percent of maintenance doses; he missed some evening doses on late session nights. His home peak flow ranges from 560 to 600 L/min. He has had no hoarseness or sore mouth. He still hopes training alone will eventually be enough. He saw the pulmonologist this morning. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Interval change</td><td>Symptoms two or three days a week; night waking once in four weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Reliever use</td><td>4 to 6 as-needed inhalations a week, mostly before training</td></tr><tr><td>Adherence</td><td>About 90 percent of maintenance doses by dose counter; evening doses missed on late nights</td></tr><tr><td>Home peak flow</td><td>560 to 600 L/min</td></tr><tr><td>Medication tolerance</td><td>No hoarseness, sore mouth, or tremor</td></tr><tr><td>Patient concern</td><td>Would prefer to rely on exercise rather than medicine</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.18"/>
    <code code="10187-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Review of systems Narrative - Reported"/>
    <title>Review of Systems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Result</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Respiratory</td><td>Positive</td><td>Mild wheeze on two or three days a week; no cough at night in the last three weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Ears, nose, mouth, and throat</td><td>Negative</td><td>No nasal blockage, sneezing, hoarseness, or sore mouth</td></tr><tr><td>Gastrointestinal</td><td>Negative</td><td>No heartburn or reflux</td></tr><tr><td>Psychiatric</td><td>Negative</td><td>Mood good; sleeping better</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>4 systems reviewed. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

