    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Moderate persistent asthma, improving (J45.40)</content>. Asthma Control Test 18, up from 13 but not yet well controlled (20 or more). The pulmonology evaluation today shows type 2 inflammation (FeNO 46 ppb, blood eosinophils 0.42 x10³/µL, total IgE 260 IU/mL) with house dust mite sensitization (8.4 kU/L). Technique errors and missed evening doses explain part of the remaining symptoms. [S]<list><item>Continue budesonide-formoterol two inhalations twice daily and one as needed, up to 12 a day.</item><item>Technique corrected today; set a phone reminder for the evening dose.</item><item>Dust-mite-impermeable mattress and pillow covers and hot washing of bedding weekly, since sensitization is now documented.</item><item>One reliever inhalation 5 to 20 minutes before boxing or rowing.</item><item>Pneumococcal vaccine PCV20 today.</item><item>Repeat spirometry at the three-month review.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Asthma Control Test</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>18, up from 13; not yet at the target of 20</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Inhaler technique with his own device</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Two critical errors corrected; correct on repeat demonstration</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Adherence and reliever use</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>About 90 percent adherence; 4 to 6 as-needed inhalations a week</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Exacerbation history</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>None since starting controller therapy</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Trigger and exposure review, smoking and vaping status</td><td>Every visit; detailed at diagnosis and yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Colds and dust are his triggers; never smoker; no vaping; no occupational exposure</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Written asthma action plan</td><td>Every visit and after every exacerbation</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Reviewed; peak-flow zones will be reset once his personal best is confirmed</td></tr><tr><td>Laboratory</td><td>FeNO, blood eosinophils, total IgE, and specific IgE</td><td>As indicated: diagnostic uncertainty, phenotyping, allergen-directed treatment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Ordered by pulmonology: FeNO 46 ppb, eosinophils 0.42 x10³/µL, total IgE 260 IU/mL, dust mite IgE 8.4 kU/L</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Pulmonology consultation</td><td>At diagnosis of uncontrolled persistent asthma</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Seen today; diagnosis confirmed and type 2 phenotype identified</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Spirometry</td><td>At diagnosis, 3 to 6 months after stabilization, then every 1 to 2 years</td><td>Due</td><td>Baseline at intake; repeat at the three-month review</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Home peak flow monitoring</td><td>Daily or with symptoms for moderate to severe asthma</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Readings 560 to 600 L/min; personal best still being established</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Step-up or step-down assessment</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Stay at Step 4; correct technique and adherence before any change</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Comorbidity surveillance: rhinitis and sinus disease, reflux, obesity, sleep apnea, vocal cord dysfunction, anxiety and depression</td><td>At diagnosis and yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>None found; BMI 23.6; PHQ-2 0 at intake; no stridor or sudden throat tightness to suggest vocal cord dysfunction</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Vaccination status</td><td>Yearly</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PCV20 given today; influenza vaccine this past autumn</td></tr><tr><td>Imaging</td><td>Chest radiograph or CT</td><td>Only for atypical features or suspected complication</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Typical asthma with reversible obstruction</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Asthma Control Test score of 20 or more by the three-month review. In progress; target 1882-06-08 [S]</item><item>FEV1 of 80 percent predicted or more on spirometry after stabilization. In progress; target 1882-06-08 [S]</item><item>No exacerbation needing oral corticosteroids over the six months after starting controller therapy. In progress; target 1882-09-14 [S]</item><item>Return to full boxing and rowing training without limiting symptoms. In progress; target 1882-06-08 [S]</item></list><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine PCV20 [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Global Strategy for Asthma Management and Prevention, 2025 update (2025); 2020 Focused Updates to the Asthma Management Guidelines: A Report from the National Asthma Education and Prevention Program Coordinating Committee Expert Panel Working Group (2020); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, asthma monograph (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Asthma review with spirometry in two months, three months after starting controller therapy. Next scheduled visit 1882-06-08: three-month asthma review with repeat spirometry. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
